<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n22938" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">indūmentum</span></b> , i, n.
		induo, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a garment</i> (post-class.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">indumenta induere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Gell. 16, 19, 12</span></i>
			: oris, <i>a mask</i>, Bass. ap. Gell.  5, 7.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>a covering</i>,
				<i>clothing</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">carnis indumenta,</span>”
				i. e. <i>bodies</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Prud. Cath. 9</span></i>
			. 99.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">indumento justitiae velare,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Lact. 6, 13, 12</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
